      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith `--tool-call-parser qwen3_coder`, a `number` parameter whose value is `1e999`, `nan`, `inf` or `-Infinity` is converted with `float()` into a Python `inf`/`nan`. `json.dumps` then writes the arguments as `{\"x\": Infinity}` or `{\"x\": NaN}`, which is not valid JSON, so strict clients fail to parse the tool call. This happens in both `detect_and_parse` and streaming.\n\n```\nschema: {\"x\": {\"type\": \"number\"}}, value: 1e999\nbefore: {\"x\": Infinity}\nafter:  {\"x\": \"1e999\"}\n```\n\nThe detector already has `_parse_finite_float`, added for union-typed parameters (#44124), but the plain `number` branch did not use it.\n\nI did not open an issue for this. I found it while checking sibling parsers after #48040, which fixes the same class of bug in `minimax_m2`. The only open PR touching `qwen3_coder_detector.py` is #41313 (string argument streaming), which does not change number conversion.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- The `number`/`float` branch of `_convert_param_value` calls `self._parse_finite_float` instead of `float`. A non-finite value raises `ValueError`, which the existing `except` handles by keeping the raw string and logging the existing warning, the same as any other value that fails to convert.\n\nFinite values are unchanged: `5` → `5`, `5.0` → `5.0`, `1e3` → `1000.0`, `-0` → `0`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable, this only changes tool-call argument parsing.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Testing\n\nCPU only (ARM Neoverse-N1), Python 3.12. Added `test_number_parameter_nonfinite_values_remain_strings` to `TestQwen3CoderDetector` in `test/registered/unit/function_call/test_function_call_parser.py`. It uses the existing `_check_structured_union_value` helper, so it covers one-shot parsing and streaming at several chunk sizes.\n\n- Without the fix the new test fails with `AssertionError: {'value': inf} != {'value': '1e999'}`.\n- With the fix, `pytest test/registered/unit/function_call/test_function_call_parser.py -k TestQwen3CoderDetector` gives 26 passed.\n- The whole file gives 253 passed and 9 failed. All 9 are in `TestDeepSeekV32Detector` and fail the same way on `main` in my environment, because `torchvision` is not installed.\n\n`pre-commit run --files` passes on both changed files.\n\nAI assistance was used to help find the issue and draft the change; I reviewed the change and ran the tests above.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). Not needed, no user-facing option changes.\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). Not applicable.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41621144059](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41621144059)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41621144014](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41621144014)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41621144042](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41621144042)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
